/** @page ssh2examplesguide Examples

    @tableofcontents

    Example of a basic sftp connection:

    @code{.py}
# create object
SFTPClient sftp("sftp://user:pass@host.com:22");
# connect to sftp server
sftp.connect();@endcode

    Example of logging in via ssh2 and executing a command and retrieving the output:

    @code{.py}
# set URL
string url = "sftp://user:pass@host.com:22";
# create object
SSH2Client ssh2(url);
# connect to remote sshd daemon
ssh2.connect();
# get a session channel
SSH2Channel chan = sc.openSessionChannel();
# execute a command on the channel
chan.exec("ls -l");
# retrieve the output and print it out
stdout.printf("%s", chan.read());
# close channel
chan.sendEof();
chan.close();
# print out the exit status after the channel is closed
stdout.printf("exit status: %d\n", chan.getExitStatus());@endcode

    Example of retrieving a file without blocking the calling thread:

    @code{.py}
SFTPClient sftp("sftp://user:pass@host.com:22");
# the operation performs the connection, authentication, and transfer without blocking
AbstractPollOperation op = sftp.startPollGetFile("/path/to/file.dat");
while (*hash<SocketPollInfo> info = op.continuePoll()) {
    # wait for the events the operation reported, along with any other I/O being managed
    Socket::poll((info,), 10s);
}
binary data = op.getOutput();@endcode

    @section ssh2verifiedexchange Verified SFTP exchange

    Use a dedicated committed directory and a private staging directory on the same filesystem. The partner must
    ensure that only complete, closed stages can enter the committed namespace. Give staging write access only to
    the publishing account. Enroll the partner's known key before connecting. A strict connection checks any
    supplied pin before authentication. Without a pin it requires an already enrolled key. The client uses
    32 KiB chunks and checks the declared length, an optional producer SHA-256, and the write and close acknowledgements.

    @par Endpoint profiles
    - <tt>openssh-posix</tt> supports <tt>replace</tt> on a qualified OpenSSH SFTP v3 endpoint with the version 1
      <tt>posix-rename@openssh.com</tt> extension. The client uses libssh2_sftp_posix_rename_ex() exclusively.
      Configure a filesystem with atomic rename and a committed directory whose writers follow the partner agreement.
      Read-only acquisition checks the producer digest supplied by a committed manifest or a trusted equivalent.
      The operator qualifies how the producer publishes on this endpoint.
    - <tt>hosted-immutable</tt> supports <tt>no-replace</tt> on a dedicated module-ssh listener serving
      <tt>SftpServerDataProvider::StagedSftpExchange</tt>. Configure the listener's SSH identification
      <tt>banner</tt> as <tt>QoreStagedSFTP_1</tt> only for accounts bound to that backend. Verify its host key
      out of band and supply the SHA-256 of the raw public key as 64 lowercase hex digits. Configure
      <tt>/staging</tt> and a single immutable filename beneath <tt>/inbound</tt>. Ordinary SFTP v3 rename then
      invokes the backend's transactional, principal-scoped uniqueness constraint. The pin, listener configuration
      and backend agreement are all required. The mapped server principal and durable server receipt can be
      obtained from the hosted backend by its operator.
    - Other profile and policy combinations return <tt>unsupported</tt>. A file listing, age, SSH identification
      string or successful trial rename cannot establish the publication agreement. The SFTP v3 ordinary rename
      packet has no collision flags. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/openssh/openssh-portable/blob/master/PROTOCOL">OpenSSH extension specification</a>
      and <a href="https://libssh2.org/libssh2_sftp_posix_rename_ex.html">libssh2 POSIX rename API</a>.

    @par Producer and consumer
    @code{.py}
    SFTPClient client("sftp://exchange@partner.example");
    client.setKnownHostsFile("/etc/exchange/known_hosts");
    client.setHostKeyPolicy(Ssh2HostKeyPolicy::Reject);
    hash<SftpExchangeSpec> spec = <SftpExchangeSpec>{
        "profile": "openssh-posix", "collision_policy": "replace",
        "staging_dir": "/outgoing/.stage", "remote_path": "/outgoing/orders-42.csv",
        "length": 3, "sha256": digest("sha256", "abc").toHex(),
    };
    hash<SftpExchangeReceipt> sent = client.publishVerified(new BinaryInputStream(binary("abc")), spec);
    if (sent.outcome == "confirmed") {
        hash<SftpExchangeReceipt> received = client.acquireVerified(spec, "/var/incoming/orders-42.csv");
        if (received.outcome != "confirmed") {
            throw "RECEIVE-FAILED", received.detail, received;
        }
    }
    @endcode
    A producer can pass a FileInputStream directly. The provider actions accept a local filename. For multipart
    deliveries, use immutable versioned member names, publish the completion manifest last, and acquire each member
    using the length and digest from that manifest. Qorus correlates members and applies the all-members gate.

    @par Reconciliation and readiness
    A confirmed receipt records the SSH endpoint, port, SSH account, host key fingerprint, absolute committed path,
    byte count and SHA-256. Within that namespace, <tt>version</tt> identifies the content by its SHA-256.
    Use distinct immutable names for logically distinct deliveries with identical bytes. A failed receipt contains
    diagnostic evidence for a definitive failure. An indeterminate receipt means the rename request may have taken
    effect. Retain the receipt and use verified acquisition or the hosted receipt store to reconcile the intended
    version before retrying. The client leaves an uncertain remote target untouched. A transport failure can leave
    a private stage for the endpoint owner to inspect and expire.

    Acquisition reads one open remote handle through EOF and publishes a mode-0600 local stage by rename in the
    destination directory. Supply an absolute local destination. Use a trusted local directory on a filesystem with atomic rename. Give concurrent
    consumers version-specific local destinations when they need independent retention. A confirm acknowledges
    visibility at commit time. Power-loss durability is a separate endpoint or filesystem agreement.

    Set the poller's <tt>commit_profile</tt>, absolute remote <tt>path</tt>, and absolute writable <tt>local_dir</tt> for
    verified events. Use <tt>hosted-immutable</tt> with <tt>/inbound</tt> and <tt>host_key_sha256</tt>, or
    <tt>openssh-sha256-name</tt> with a committed directory containing names of the form
    <tt>lowercase-sha256.logical-name</tt>. Each file event carries the receipt after local publication. Repeated
    discovery yields the same identity for the same committed version. Keep legacy integration settings to retain
    the existing polling behavior.

    @par Qualification
    From the module checkout run <tt>python3 test/atomic-exchange/run.py --build build-debug</tt>. The fixture creates
    a loopback OpenSSH listener with temporary keys and controls close, read and rename replies. Add the companion
    module's <tt>qlib</tt> and native build directory to <tt>QORE_MODULE_DIR</tt> to include the SQLite-backed
    hosted listener. Pass <tt>--valgrind</tt> for native memory checks.
*/
